+/* Shallow WALL schedule: already-stretched PCM on the player node. This is the
+ * only "old rate" residual on changeRate — keep short so hold feels instant. */
+static const double kAVAEMaxWallSec = 0.25;
+/* Wall buffers the player node can hold at once: 250 ms of wall at the
+ * smallest chunk the feed produces is far below this. Overflow drops the
+ * oldest entry, which the node has already played back. */
+enum { kAVAEWallRingCapacity = 256 };
+/* Deep RAW content reserve (rate-agnostic). Must cover full inter-arrival of
+ * bursty demux/aout (~5s measured) plus margin so 1× never drains to underrun
+ * between segment-cadence feeds. At 2×, content drains 2× into wall — bank
+ * still rate-agnostic (frames of content, not wall). Not a 0007 decoder cap.
+ * FEED-FIX K2.3: raised 2s→8s after FEED-DIAG cyclic underrun proof.
+ * FEED-FIX K2.4: raised 8s→12s so healthy 1× prefill has more 2× runway. */
+static const double kAVAEMaxRawSec = 12.00;
+/* Absolute safety ceiling only. Accept freely under MaxRaw; accept with
+ * RAW_HIGH warn between MaxRaw and HardRaw; DROP newest only above HardRaw
+ * (should be rare if 1× consume continues). Memory: stereo f32 @48k ≈
+ * 18s * 48000 * 8 ≈ 6.9 MiB — fine on device.
+ * FEED-FIX K2.4: raised 12s→18s with MaxRaw=12s. */
+static const double kAVAEHardRawSec = 18.00;
+static const float kAVAEHeadroom = 0.707f;
+static const float kAVAEUnityEpsilon = 0.001f;
